### An off switch for dual-use knowledge in AI models
- [[off-switch-gram]] - Gradient-Routed Auxiliary Modules (GRAM) methodology for surgically removing dual-use knowledge while preserving general performance
  - Structural "off switch" that physically isolates and removes capability weights
  - Resists restoration via fine-tuning far better than standard unlearning
  - Requires architectural intervention at training time with auxiliary modules
  - **Activation**: GRAM, gradient-routed auxiliary modules, off switch for dual-use knowledge, surgical capability removal